# CODEOWNERS — Tier-1 / Tier-2 review model.
#
# Goal: concentrate the scarce non-author approver on the small set of
# CONSENSUS-CRITICAL paths where a bad merge is unrecoverable, and let
# everything else clear on CI + Codex + a single LGTM. This keeps the
# reviewer off the critical path of docs / tooling / devnet / EVM-glue.
#
# This file only GATES merges when the `main` ruleset sets
# `require_code_owner_review: true`. Until then it is advisory
# (auto-requests review). Flipping that on is the governance step that
# makes Tier-1 below mandatory.
#
# Syntax: <path-pattern>  <@handle> [<@handle> ...]; either listed owner
# satisfies the rule. Both maintainers are listed on every Tier-1 path so
# the *other* one is always an eligible non-author reviewer (the branch
# ruleset forbids self-approval), and so neither maintainer's own Tier-1
# PR deadlocks. Later rules override earlier ones for the same path.
#
# NOTE: there is intentionally NO `*` catch-all. Paths not listed here
# have no code owner and therefore do NOT require code-owner review —
# that is the Tier-2 velocity path (CI + Codex + one approval).

# === Tier-1: consensus / crypto / parity / recovery — REQUIRED owner ===

